wp:postmeta.wp:meta_value:
[{"nav_label": "Extensions", "title": "Extensions", "media": "", "copy": "<span class="eyebrow">Extending</span>


  <p>Everything in <code>extensions/</code> is auto-discovered. Drop a correctly-named file into the right folder and it is picked up — there is no registry to edit, and no core file changes, so the framework stays upgradeable.</p>

  <div class="code">
    <span class="lang">extensions/</span>
<pre>extensions/
├── api/
│   ├── classes/post-types/   <span class="c"># class-{slug}.php  → post type classes</span>
│   └── *.php                 <span class="c"># flat includes: routes, helpers, hooks</span>
└── app/
    ├── components/
    │   ├── panels/           <span class="c"># PascalCase.tsx → panel components</span>
    │   └── templates/single/ <span class="c"># PascalCase.tsx → single-post templates</span>
    └── styles/
        └── extensions-global.scss</pre>
  </div>

  <div class="tablewrap">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Add a…</th><th>Put it here</th><th>Discovered by</th><th>Key becomes</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Post type</td><td class="mono">extensions/api/classes/post-types/<b>class-case-study.php</b></td><td><code>glob()</code> on <code>after_setup_theme</code> (priority 0)</td><td>—</td></tr>
        <tr><td>REST route or helper</td><td class="mono">extensions/api/<b>routes.php</b></td><td><code>glob()</code> at include time</td><td>—</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Panel</td><td class="mono">extensions/app/components/panels/<b>CustomStats.tsx</b></td><td><code>import.meta.glob()</code></td><td><code>custom-stats</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Single template</td><td class="mono">extensions/app/components/templates/single/<b>CaseStudy.tsx</b></td><td><code>import.meta.glob()</code></td><td><code>case-study</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Styles</td><td class="mono">extensions/app/styles/<b>extensions-global.scss</b></td><td>Vite entry</td><td>—</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="note">
    <span class="label">Precedence</span>
    <p>A core panel or template with the same key always wins. Extensions can add new types; they cannot override built-in ones. Extension post type classes load immediately after core ones, so <code>DO_Custom_Post_Type</code> always exists to extend.</p>
  </div>

  <h3>Registering a panel type with the CMS</h3>
  <p>Auto-discovery handles the React side. To make the panel <em>selectable in wp-admin</em>, register its key through the <code>devo_panel_types</code> filter — never by editing <code>class-landing-page.php</code>:</p>

  <div class="code">
    <span class="lang">php &middot; extensions/api/panels.php</span>
<pre>add_filter( <span class="s">'devo_panel_types'</span>, <span class="k">function</span>( $panel_types ) {
    $panel_types[<span class="s">'custom-stats'</span>] = [
        <span class="s">'label'</span> => <span class="s">'Custom Stats'</span>,
        <span class="s">'value'</span> => <span class="s">'custom-stats'</span>,
    ];
    <span class="k">return</span> $panel_types;
} );</pre>
  </div>

  <p>The <code>value</code> must match the kebab-case key derived from the component filename, or the panel will be selectable but render nothing.</p>

  <h3>Single templates</h3>
  <p>The template's key must match the post type's <code>rest_slug</code> (falling back to <code>slug</code>), because <code>TemplateLoader</code> matches on the value returned by the REST API. A <code>devo_case_study</code> post type with <code>'rest_slug' =&gt; 'case-study'</code> pairs with <code>CaseStudy.tsx</code>.</p>", "cta": ""}, {"nav_label": "Worked example", "title": "Worked example: a new panel", "media": "", "copy": "<span class="eyebrow">Extending</span>


  <p>Adding a &ldquo;Timeline&rdquo; panel, end to end. No core file is touched.</p>

  <h4>1 — Declare the fields</h4>
  <p>Register the panel type and its fields from a flat extension include.</p>

  <div class="code">
    <span class="lang">php &middot; extensions/api/timeline-panel.php</span>
<pre><span class="c">// Make the type selectable in the Panel Type dropdown.</span>
add_filter( <span class="s">'devo_panel_types'</span>, <span class="k">function</span>( $types ) {
    $types[<span class="s">'timeline'</span>] = [ <span class="s">'label'</span> => <span class="s">'Timeline'</span>, <span class="s">'value'</span> => <span class="s">'timeline'</span> ];
    <span class="k">return</span> $types;
} );

<span class="c">// Give it fields. Merged in when 'timeline' is the selected Panel Type.</span>
add_filter( <span class="s">'devo_panel_fields'</span>, <span class="k">function</span>( $fields ) {
    $fields[<span class="s">'timeline'</span>] = [
        <span class="s">'Title'</span>      => <span class="s">'text'</span>,
        <span class="s">'Background'</span> => <span class="s">'background'</span>,
        <span class="s">'Copy'</span>       => <span class="s">'wp_editor'</span>,
        <span class="s">'ID'</span>         => <span class="s">'varchar'</span>,
        <span class="s">'Events'</span>     => [
            <span class="s">'type'</span>   => <span class="s">'multi_array'</span>,
            <span class="s">'fields'</span> => [
                <span class="s">'Year'</span>  => <span class="s">'varchar'</span>,
                <span class="s">'Title'</span> => <span class="s">'text'</span>,
                <span class="s">'Copy'</span>  => <span class="s">'html'</span>,
                <span class="s">'Media'</span> => <span class="s">'media'</span>,
            ],
        ],
    ];
    <span class="k">return</span> $fields;
} );</pre>
  </div>

  <div class="note caution">
    <span class="label">Check before you copy</span>
    <p>Panel <em>types</em> are filterable through <code>devo_panel_types</code> as shipped. Panel <em>fields</em> are assembled by <code>DO_Landing_Page::set_panel_fields()</code>, which is not filtered in the current code. Either add a <code>devo_panel_fields</code> filter to that method — a one-line change, and the cleaner option — or subclass <code>DO_Landing_Page</code> in your extension and override <code>set_panel_fields()</code> to merge your entry in.</p>
  </div>

  <h4>2 — Build the component</h4>
  <p>The filename determines the key: <code>Timeline.tsx</code> &rarr; <code>timeline</code>.</p>

  <div class="code">
    <span class="lang">tsx &middot; extensions/app/components/panels/Timeline.tsx</span>
<pre><span class="k">import</span> React <span class="k">from</span> <span class="s">'react'</span>;
<span class="k">import</span> { getArrayField, parse } <span class="k">from</span> <span class="s">'@/utils/helpers'</span>;
<span class="k">import</span> { PanelProps } <span class="k">from</span> <span class="s">'@/utils/types/PanelProps'</span>;
<span class="k">import</span> { Media } <span class="k">from</span> <span class="s">'@/utils/types/Media'</span>;

<span class="k">interface</span> TimelineEvent { year: string; title: string; copy: string; media?: Media; }

<span class="k">const</span> Timeline: React.FC&lt;PanelProps&gt; = ( { post, panelPrefix = <span class="s">''</span>, panelSuffix = <span class="s">''</span> } ) =&gt; {
    <span class="k">const</span> events = getArrayField&lt;TimelineEvent&gt;(
        post.fields,
        `${ panelPrefix }_events${ panelSuffix }`
    );

    <span class="k">if</span> ( ! events.length ) {
        <span class="k">return null</span>;
    }

    <span class="k">return</span> (
        &lt;ol className=<span class="s">"timeline"</span>&gt;
            { events.map( ( event, i ) =&gt; (
                &lt;li className=<span class="s">"timeline__item"</span> key={ i }&gt;
                    &lt;p className=<span class="s">"timeline__year"</span>&gt;{ event.year }&lt;/p&gt;
                    &lt;h3 className=<span class="s">"timeline__title"</span>&gt;{ event.title }&lt;/h3&gt;
                    &lt;div className=<span class="s">"timeline__copy"</span>&gt;{ parse( event.copy ) }&lt;/div&gt;
                &lt;/li&gt;
            ) ) }
        &lt;/ol&gt;
    );
};
<span class="k">export default</span> Timeline;</pre>
  </div>

  <p>Note what the component does <em>not</em> do: it renders no panel wrapper, heading or background. <code>Panel</code> and <code>PanelWrapper</code> have already handled the title, copy, background classes and anchor ID. The panel component is responsible only for its own distinctive content.</p>

  <h4>3 — Style it</h4>
  <p>Structural rules go in <code>app/styles/components/</code> and are imported by the component; visual treatment goes in the extensions layer, nested under <code>#root</code>.</p>

  <div class="code">
    <span class="lang">scss &middot; extensions/app/styles/components/_timeline.scss</span>
<pre>@use <span class="s">'../abstracts'</span> as *;

#root {
    ol.timeline {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 40px;
        border-left: 1px solid var(--devo-rule);
        padding-left: 32px;

        li.timeline__item { position: relative; }

        p.timeline__year {
            @include mono-label(12px);
            color: var(--devo-accent);
        }

        h3.timeline__title {
            @include display(28px);
            margin: 6px 0 10px;
        }
    }
}</pre>
  </div>

  <p>Then add <code>@use 'components/timeline';</code> to <code>extensions-global.scss</code>.</p>

  <div class="note caution">
    <span class="label">Easy to miss</span>
    <p>A partial in <code>components/</code> that is never <code>@use</code>d compiles to nothing and fails silently. <code>_demo-annotations.scss</code> is currently in exactly that state — present, edited, and not imported by <code>extensions-global.scss</code>.</p>
  </div>

  <h4>4 — Build and use</h4>
  <p>Run <code>npm run build</code>. In wp-admin, add a panel, choose <em>Timeline</em>, and the fields from step 1 appear.</p>", "cta": ""}, {"nav_label": "For editors", "title": "Guide for editors", "media": "", "copy": "<span class="eyebrow">Using the CMS</span>


  <h3>Building a landing page</h3>
  <ol class="body-list">
    <li>Create a <strong>Landing Page</strong>. Fill in <strong>Title</strong> and <strong>Slug</strong> — the slug becomes the URL directly off the site root, so <code>about-us</code> gives <code>/about-us/</code>.</li>
    <li>Complete the <strong>Hero</strong> box: title, background, copy and CTA. It always renders first.</li>
    <li>Set <strong>Panel Count</strong> to the number of sections you want. Save. That many numbered Panel boxes appear.</li>
    <li>In each panel, choose a <strong>Panel Type</strong> and save — the fields for that type appear.</li>
    <li>Fill in the <strong>SEO</strong> box. SEO Title overrides the page Title for search engines; SEO Description overrides the hero Copy. Character counters show the recommended limits: 60 for titles, 160 for descriptions.</li>
  </ol>

  <div class="note">
    <span class="label">Reordering and removing panels</span>
    <p>Panel content is stored against the panel's <em>number</em>. Reducing Panel Count hides the trailing panels but does not delete their data — raise the count again and the content returns. To reorder, move the field values, not the boxes.</p>
  </div>

  <h3>Panel controls available on every panel</h3>
  <div class="tablewrap tight">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td class="mono"><b>Hide Panel</b></td><td>Removes the panel from the page without losing its content.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono"><b>Title</b></td><td>Panel heading. Also becomes the anchor ID if none is set.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono"><b>Background</b></td><td>Image or video, colour, and overlay. Video backgrounds add player controls automatically.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono"><b>Copy</b></td><td>Intro text above the panel's content.</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="mono"><b>ID</b></td><td>Explicit anchor, for linking to <code>/page/#your-id</code>.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h3>Field-specific rules worth knowing</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Stats numbers</strong> must be bare numbers — no commas, currency symbols or suffixes. Formatting and count-up animation are applied on the front end.</li>
    <li><strong>Internal CTA links</strong> take a path only, not a full URL — <code>blog</code>, not <code>https://example.com/blog</code>. This keeps navigation client-side and instant.</li>
    <li><strong>Gallery images</strong> require a Title for screen-reader text. A URL is honoured only when the image is not opening in a lightbox.</li>
    <li><strong>Search Subject</strong> — if you preset one, the subject filter will not appear for visitors.</li>
    <li><strong>Frame</strong> fields accept square-bracket syntax only: <code>[iframe][/iframe]</code>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Admin conveniences</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>The admin colour scheme tells you which environment you are in — purple for local, blue for dev, light for staging, dark for production.</li>
    <li>List tables show 200 rows per page rather than 20.</li>
    <li>URLs are case-insensitive: any uppercase path redirects to lowercase.</li>
    <li>The Media Library has an <strong>Icons</strong> tab, filtered to the icon library.</li>
  </ul>", "cta": ""}]
